In 2026, several outlets headlined the Bentz &amp; Dutkiewicz PNAS study of Aurignacian engraved marks as the discovery of a 40,000-year-old writing system that predates Mesopotamia — e.g. 'engraved signs ... constitute a 40,000-year-old writing system predating the Mesopotamian one'.

Earliest attestation: labrujulaverde.com, February 2026: 'Engraved signs on the Adorant and other Stone Age artifacts constitute a 40,000-year-old writing system predating the Mesopotamian one'
Sources: The telling: labrujulaverde.com headline asserting a 40,000-year-old writing system predating Mesopotamia; The study's own conclusion (via ScienceAlert, Feb 2026): the Aurignacian marks 'are not complex enough to qualify as writing in the strict sense — they do not directly represent spoken language'; structural features comparable to proto-cuneiform, not writing itself; The graded study record: evt-swabian-jura-notation-2026-001 CORROBORATED — the structured notational system and its statistical properties; the grade explicitly does NOT certify the marks as writing
Falsifiability: A demonstration that the Aurignacian marks encode spoken language (phonetic or syntactic structure tied to speech)</description><styleUrl>#debunked</styleUrl><TimeStamp><when>2026-01-01</when></TimeStamp><Point><coordinates>9.7667,48.3833,0</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData><Data name="grade"><value>DEBUNKED</value></Data><Data name="layer"><value>fake</value></Data><Data name="year"><value>2026</value></Data><Data name="weight"><value>0.6</value></Data></ExtendedData></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The October 2026 '100% confirmed' Durupınar telling</name><description>Grade: DEBUNKED — The telling's own cited evidence refutes it: the team's researcher Andrew Jones (reported via answeredfaith.com from the Charisma/Western Journal coverage) 'acknowledged it is too early to claim he has found evidence that the ark itself is buried there' — the headline claims more than the researcher; the lab results (366 samples, carbon-isotope and age determination) are still pending winter 2026-27; no peer-reviewed publication exists; the dissent comes from inside the creationist camp (Snelling, Answers in Genesis: location/geology rule it out); and the 1996 natural-formation reading is unrefuted. The grade kills the confirmation-claim, never the drilling, never the pending labs, never the flood question.
